    <briefdescription>
<para>Concept satisfied by a callable object that can be the body of a test case. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The body is stored decayed, and invoked as an lvalue with a <computeroutput>test_case&amp;</computeroutput> reference as the first argument, followed by the stored arguments, as lvalues, as <computeroutput>bind_callable()</computeroutput> invokes it. A body that does not satisfy it, for example a lambda with the wrong parameters, is rejected at the call of <computeroutput>test()</computeroutput>, not inside the framework. The generic callables (see <computeroutput>generic_callable</computeroutput>) are accepted without the check.</para>
